    {
      "claim_id": "L020",
      "reason": "Cefotaxime substitution is suggested, yet none of the provided NICE passages endorse cefotaxime as an alternative for penicillin allergy."
    }
  ],
  "critical_omissions": [
    "The plan does not include vancomycin, which NICE S007 recommends as the primary alternative for severe penicillin allergy.",
    "Duration of antibiotic therapy is not aligned with NICE S005/S010 recommendations (7 days or stop at 36 h if culture negative and low risk)."
  ],
  "regimen_incomplete": true,
  "rationale": "Risk assessment and need for antibiotics are supported (S003, S015). Blood culture and CRP monitoring follow S006 and S009. However, the antibiotic regimen lacks NICE‑supported alternatives for penicillin allergy (S007) and includes clindamycin/cefotaxime without citation, and omits recommended treatment duration (S005, S010)."
}
